    "title": "Boston Celtics vs. Phoenix Suns: Stream, lineups, injury reports, broadcast (3/16)",
    "text": "Updated March 16, 2026, 2:39 p.m. ETThe Boston Celtics will play host to a Western Conference foe as they host the Phoenix Suns at TD Garden this Monday (March 16) night. The Celtics are going to be looking to stay in the win column after righting the ship vs. an East opponent earlier this week. On the other side of the court, the Suns will be looking to get back in the win column to begin with after losing a contest to an East foe in their last game.We expect a Celtics win, but this version of Phoenix is not a team you can mail a contest in against, so be wary of Boston playing down to a perceived lesser foe.Records, standing, and streaksAt present, the Celtics have a 44-23 record, which has them second in the Eastern Conference standings.The Suns are the owners of a 39-28 record, good enough for seventh in the West.What happened in the last game for each team?Boston beat the Washington Wizards 111-100 at home.Phoenix lost to the Toronto Raptors 122-115 on the road.InjuriesFor Boston, Nikola Vucevic (hand) is out.For Phoenix, Dillon Brooks (hand) and Mark Williams (foot) are out.Probable starting lineups - CelticsDerrick WhiteJaylen BrownSam HauserJayson TatumNeemias QuetaProbable starting lineups - SunsRoyce O'NealeOso IghodaroDevin BookerCollin GillespieJalen GreenWhat time is tipoff, and on what channels?Here's when you should tune in to see the game:Date: 3/16Time: 7:30 p.m. ETTV Channel: NBC Sports BostonLive Stream: Fubo (watch for free)Listen to \"Havlicek Stole the Pod\" on:Blue Wire: https://tiny.ee/CdKpiTunes: https://tiny.ee/RK47YouTube: https://tiny.ee/cOW3",
